## Why This Is Asked

This question tests understanding of augmented binary search trees to support order statistics—a fundamental data structures concept.

## Key Concepts

- **Augmented BST/Treap**: Each node stores value, count (for duplicates), and subtreeSize
- **Order statistics**: getKthSmallest navigates using left subtree size and node counts
- **Duplicate handling**: Multiple identical values stored in a single node with a count field
- **Rebalancing**: Operations maintain O(log n) time via rotations or split/merge

## Code Example

```javascript
class Node {
  constructor(v) {
    this.v = v;
    this.c = 1;      // count of this value
    this.sz = 1;     // subtree size
    this.l = null;
    this.r = null;
    this.p = null;  // priority for treap
  }

  upd() {
    this.sz = (this.l?.sz || 0) + (this.r?.sz || 0) + this.c;
  }
}

function kth(node, k) {
  if (!node) return null;
  const leftSize = node.l?.sz || 0;
  if (k <= leftSize) return kth(node.l, k);
  if (k <= leftSize + node.c) return node.v;
  return kth(node.r, k - leftSize - node.c);
}
```

## Time Complexity

- Insert: O(log n)
- EraseOne: O(log n)
- GetKthSmallest: O(log n)

## Why This Is Asked

Evaluates practical data-structure composition: a queue with constant-time min tracking, a common interview pattern for streams and real-time dashboards.

## Key Concepts

- Two-stack queue pattern
- Per-stack min tracking
- Amortized analysis and edge-case handling for duplicates

## Code Example

```javascript
class MinQueue {
  constructor(){ this.inStack = []; this.outStack = []; }
  enqueue(x){ const minIn = this.inStack.length ? Math.min(x, this.inStack[this.inStack.length-1][1]) : x; this.inStack.push([x, minIn]); }
  dequeue(){ if (!this.outStack.length){ while (this.inStack.length){ const [val] = this.inStack.pop(); const minOut = this.outStack.length ? Math.min(val, this.outStack[this.outStack.length-1][1]) : val; this.outStack.push([val, minOut]); } }
    const popped = this.outStack.pop(); return popped ? popped[0] : undefined; }
  getMin(){ const minIn = this.inStack.length ? this.inStack[this.inStack.length-1][1] : Infinity; const minOut = this.outStack.length ? this.outStack[this.outStack.length-1][1] : Infinity; return Math.min(minIn, minOut); }
}
```

